  "title": "2026-09-08-comp-134600 · eval-harness-orchestration",
  "description": "# Offline evaluation harness orchestration\nRead left to right: an immutable pinned suite and run fingerprint feed a scheduler and bounded worker pool against an isolated SUT, never production. Workers execute ordered steps and capture full transcripts, final artifacts and typed failure records. Infrastructure faults are recorded and retried; behavior failures are recorded before continuing.\n\nEach completed scenario immediately enters globally bounded concurrent grading. Independent criterion graders and an artifact-only grader (without the original request) produce verdicts requiring evidence. Missing evidence invalidates a verdict; retry once, flag repeated failure, and assemble only valid verdicts.\n\nThe assembler builds a scorecard. Comparison with the chosen baseline requires identical fingerprints; compatible movements crossing the threshold are narrated, while incompatible comparisons are blocked. Promotion sets the baseline for future compatible runs. The audit archive retains every artifact, transcript and verdict, including invalid attempts and typed faults, for review. Scenario wording changes create new versions rather than altering frozen definitions.",
